      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Family members are the patient's blood relatives on both sides of the family whose health histories are collected for the family history. The care team asks about their diseases and genetic testing, as well as health issues such as heart disease, cancer, and diabetes, which are all relevant to understanding the patient's familial risk. Beyond their role in medical history, family members also provide practical and emotional support, including transportation, meals, emotional encouragement, and help taking notes during appointments.
**Relationships:** (No explicit relationships listed in the data tables)</data>
