    <node id="MAMMOGRAM">
      <data key="d0">MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d1">MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">MAMMOGRAM is an imaging test that produces an x-ray picture of the inside of the breast using low-dose x-rays. It may be performed as a standard 2D digital mammogram or as a 3D mammogram, known as tomosynthesis. The mammogram is used both for breast cancer screening and for the evaluation or diagnosis of breast conditions. It is interpreted by a breast diagnostic radiologist. In addition to screening and diagnosis, a mammogram can also be used to guide a biopsy; when used in this way, the procedure is called a stereotactic needle biopsy.
Relationships:
  - Source: BREAST CANCER SCREENING
  - Target: MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: Mammograms are imaging tests used in breast cancer screening
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: A mammogram is an imaging examination used to examine breast tissue. A diagnostic mammogram is a specific type of mammogram performed when there are symptoms or abnormal findings that require further evaluation. Specifically, diagnostic mammograms are used to assess symptoms such as a lump, pain, or nipple discharge, or to follow up on abnormal results from a routine screening mammogram. In essence, while a screening mammogram is used for early detection in asymptomatic individuals, a diagnostic mammogram is a focused examination intended to clarify and evaluate suspicious signs or prior screening abnormalities, providing more detailed imaging to aid in diagnosis.
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: MAMMOGRAM SCREENING
  - Description: Mammogram screening is the use of mammograms to screen for breast cancer
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: SCREENING MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: A mammogram is a medical imaging procedure used to examine breast tissue. A screening mammogram is a specific type of mammogram that is performed regularly as a routine preventive measure, even when the individual has no symptoms or signs of breast disease. Screening mammograms are conducted on a scheduled basis, typically for early detection of breast abnormalities, including cancer, in asymptomatic individuals.
  - Source: BREAST MRI
  - Target: MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: A breast MRI may be used in addition to a mammogram
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: DIGITAL MAMMOGRAPHY
  - Description: Digital mammography is a standard 2D mammogram technique
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: TOMOSYNTHESIS
  - Description: Tomosynthesis is a 3D mammogram technique
  - Source: BREAST CANCER
  - Target: MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: Mammograms are used to image and screen for breast cancer
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: MRI
  - Description: Mammograms and MRIs are imaging tests interpreted by a breast diagnostic radiologist
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: EARLY DETECTION
  - Description: Mammograms are used for early detection of breast cancer
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: Mammogram can be used to guide a biopsy.
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: ULTRASOUND
  - Description: Mammograms and ultrasound are imaging tests used in breast cancer evaluation
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
