    <node id="SMOKEFREE.GOV">
      <data key="d0">SMOKEFREE.GOV</data>
      <data key="d1">SMOKEFREE.GOV</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">SmokeFree.gov is a website recognized as an online support resource for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. It is listed alongside CDC.gov/tobacco as a recommended online smoking/vaping cessation support resource. 
**Relationships:**
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Description: Both are recommended online smoking/vaping cessation support resources. 
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both recognized as recommended online resources for quitting smoking and vaping. They are frequently listed together as credible, web-based smoking cessation support options, providing individuals with accessible tools and information to help them stop using tobacco products or e-cigarettes. Both websites serve as authoritative sources of guidance for those seeking to quit. 
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support option to help people quit smoking or vaping, while the CDC’s website, CDC.gov/tobacco, is also listed as an online support resource for quitting tobacco. Together, they serve as accessible digital tools for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and assistance to those looking to stop using tobacco products. 

---</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BETOBACCOFREE.GOV">
      <data key="d0">BETOBACCOFREE.GOV</data>
      <data key="d1">BETOBACCOFREE.GOV</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">BeTobaccoFree.gov is a website recognized as an online support resource for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. It is listed alongside CDC.gov/tobacco as a recommended smoking cessation support resource. 
**Relationships:**
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both online support websites designed to help individuals quit smoking or vaping. They are recommended smoking cessation support resources and are frequently listed together in guidance as trusted online options for quitting tobacco use. Both websites serve as accessible, evidence-based quit-smoking and quit-vaping support tools, often cited side by side for individuals seeking help with nicotine addiction. 
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, the CDC provides these resources through its dedicated website, CDC.gov/tobacco. Together, BeTobaccoFree.gov and the CDC serve as accessible online support options to help people quit smoking or vaping. Both entities are listed as credible sources of assistance for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and resources for those looking to stop using tobacco products. 

