  - Target: NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE
  - Description: The National Cancer Institute (NCI) and NCCN Cancer Centers are both U.S. organizations listed as resources for finding cancer clinical trials. They serve as authoritative sources for locating clinical trials available in the United States. NCCN Cancer Centers can be accessed online at NCCN.org/cancercenters, while the NCI’s corresponding resource is available at cancer.gov. Both are recognized for providing information on cancer clinical trials to patients, caregivers, and researchers. 

