    <node id="U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE">
      <data key="d0">U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE</data>
      <data key="d1">U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) is a U.S. government medical library and organization. It maintains and operates ClinicalTrials.gov, a comprehensive clinical trial registry and search database used for finding clinical trials worldwide. Through this resource, the NLM provides researchers, healthcare professionals, and the public with access to information on clinical trials conducted across the globe. 
**Relationships:**
  - Source: NCCN CANCER CENTERS
  - Target: U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE
  - Description: NCCN Cancer Centers and the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) are both recognized resources for locating clinical trials. NCCN Cancer Centers are specifically listed as a resource for finding clinical trials within the United States, while the NLM provides the worldwide clinicaltrials.gov database. Together, these two entities offer complementary access to clinical trial information: NCCN Cancer Centers focus on U.S.-based cancer centers, and the NLM supplies a comprehensive, global database of clinical trials. 

---</data>
