      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">Anal cancer, also known as anal canal cancer, is an uncommon cancer of the digestive system. It most often originates in the squamous cells that line the anal canal or the perianal region. As the cancer being treated, anal cancer can be classified as stage I, II, or III, and the standard treatment approach involves chemoradiation.
