  - Target: SPINAL TAP
  - Description: A lumbar puncture, also known as a spinal tap, is a medical procedure. Both names—lumbar puncture and spinal tap—refer to the same diagnostic and therapeutic technique. The procedure involves inserting a needle into the lower back to access the subarachnoid space in order to collect cerebrospinal fluid for analysis, measure pressure, or administer medication. It is performed by a trained healthcare professional and is commonly used to help diagnose conditions affecting the central nervous system, such as infections, inflammation, or bleeding.</data>
