    <node id="FERTILITY AND FAMILY PLANNING">
      <data key="d0">FERTILITY AND FAMILY PLANNING</data>
      <data key="d1">FERTILITY AND FAMILY PLANNING</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">Fertility and family planning is an important supportive care topic for cancer patients, addressing the reproductive health challenges that can arise from cancer treatment. Specifically, fertility and family planning counseling is designed to help individuals understand the fertility-related risks associated with cancer therapies and explore options for preserving fertility. This is particularly relevant for young adults diagnosed with colon cancer, as treatments may impact their ability to conceive or bear children in the future. The counseling aims to provide education and guidance on fertility preservation methods, allowing patients to make informed decisions before, during, and after treatment.

In addition to its role for colon cancer patients, fertility and family planning is also recognized as a key topic in patient education materials for people with anal cancer. The inclusion of this subject in patient guides for anal cancer underscores its broad applicability across different cancer types, ensuring that all patients have access to information about how their treatment may affect fertility and what family planning options are available.

Overall, fertility and family planning encompasses both medical counseling and informational resources, helping cancer patients navigate the complex intersection of oncology and reproductive health. By integrating this topic into cancer care, healthcare providers can better support patients' long-term quality of life and reproductive autonomy.
Relationships:
  - Source: FERTILITY AND FAMILY PLANNING
  - Target: COLON CANCER
  - Description: Young adults diagnosed with colon cancer should be counseled about fertility risks and preservation options.</data>
    </node>
