    <node id="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION">
      <data key="d0">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION</data>
      <data key="d1">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">Digital rectal examination (DRE) is a physical exam event used in the follow-up care of patients who have received chemoradiation. It is recommended as an initial follow-up examination 8 to 12 weeks after completing chemoradiation, specifically to check the results of the treatment. Beyond this early assessment, the DRE also plays a role in longer-term surveillance: it is typically performed every 3 to 6 months for 5 years after treatment. Thus, the digital rectal examination serves both as a short-term response evaluation and as a routine monitoring tool during post-treatment surveillance.
Relationships:
  - Source: SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION
  - Description: Digital rectal examination is a recommended component of surveillance after treatment
  - Source: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Target: DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION
  - Description: The physical exam is performed together with digital rectal examination.
  - Source: DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION
  - Target: ANOSCOPY
  - Description: Digital rectal examination and anoscopy are recommended together during the follow-up exam.
  - Source: CHEMORADIATION
  - Target: DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION
  - Description: Digital rectal examination is recommended 8 to 12 weeks after completing chemoradiation.
  - Source: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION
  - Description: Follow-up and surveillance includes digital rectal examination.</data>
    </node>
