  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Target: UTERINE CANCER
  - Description: Both are gynecologic cancers mentioned in the same diagnostic discussion of suspected ovarian cancer, although they are detected or ruled out by different tests.
  - Source: UTERINE CANCER
  - Target: ENDOMETRIAL BIOPSY
  - Description: An endometrial biopsy can rule out uterine cancer.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAP TEST">
      <data key="d0">PAP TEST</data>
      <data key="d1">PAP TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">The Pap test (also known as Pap smear or cervical/vaginal cytology) is a medical screening procedure in which a sample of cells is removed from the cervix during a pelvic exam. It is primarily used to detect cervical cancer or precancerous changes in the cervix, and it is not used to detect ovarian cancer. After treatment for cervical cancer, the Pap test is typically performed as an annual screening test to identify abnormal or precancerous cells. However, while it is useful for this purpose, it is not highly effective at detecting recurrent cervical cancer. Thus, the Pap test remains a key tool for initial cervical cancer screening and post-treatment surveillance, despite its limitations in detecting recurrence.
Relationships:
  - Source: PELVIC EXAM
  - Target: PAP TEST
  - Description: A sample of cells for the Pap test may be removed during the pelvic exam.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECTOVAGINAL EXAM">
      <data key="d0">RECTOVAGINAL EXAM</data>
      <data key="d1">RECTOVAGINAL EXAM</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">An exam of the rectum and vagina together to check for cancer in the space between the rectum and vagina.
Relationships:
  - Source: PELVIC EXAM
  - Target: RECTOVAGINAL EXAM
  - Description: A rectovaginal exam may be done during the pelvic evaluation to check for cancer between the rectum and vagina.
  - Source: OVARIAN CANCER
  - Target: RECTOVAGINAL EXAM
  - Description: The rectovaginal exam is performed to check for cancer in the space between the rectum and vagina.</data>
    </node>
