    <node id="MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE">
      <data key="d0">MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE</data>
      <data key="d1">MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Multidisciplinary care is a coordinated healthcare approach in which doctors, specialists, and allied health providers work and communicate as a single, cohesive team. This collaborative model is centered on planning and delivering a patient’s diagnosis and treatment, with the overarching goal of helping the patient through integrated, team-based care. Rather than operating in silos, the various professionals share information and coordinate their efforts to ensure that all aspects of a patient’s condition are addressed comprehensively. By bringing together diverse clinical expertise, multidisciplinary care aims to improve the quality, safety, and effectiveness of patient management, ensuring that diagnostic and therapeutic decisions are made collectively and tailored to the individual’s needs.
Relationships:
  - Source: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE
  - Description: The multidisciplinary team coordinates chemotherapy as part of the treatment plan.
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE
  - Description: The multidisciplinary team discusses treatment options including clinical trials with the patient.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE
Description: Multidisciplinary care is a coordinated healthcare approach in which doctors, specialists, and allied health providers work and communicate as a single, cohesive team. This collaborative model is centered on planning and delivering a patient’s diagnosis and treatment, with the overarching goal of helping the patient through integrated, team-based care. Rather than operating in silos, the various professionals share information and coordinate their efforts to ensure that all aspects of a patient’s condition are addressed comprehensively. By bringing together diverse clinical expertise, multidisciplinary care aims to improve the quality, safety, and effectiveness of patient management, ensuring that diagnostic and therapeutic decisions are made collectively and tailored to the individual’s needs.
Relationships:
  - Source: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE
  - Description: The multidisciplinary team coordinates chemotherapy as part of the treatment plan.
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
