    </node>
    <node id="RESEARCH TEAM">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH TEAM</data>
      <data key="d1">RESEARCH TEAM</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The RESEARCH TEAM is a group of experts responsible for managing clinical trials. Their duties include reviewing the study with participants, explaining the study's purpose, risks, and benefits, as well as collecting research data and coordinating care for patients who are participating in the clinical trial.
Relationships:
  - Source: CARE TEAM
  - Target: RESEARCH TEAM
  - Description: The research team is part of the broader care team for patients in a clinical trial
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIALS
  - Target: RESEARCH TEAM
  - Description: Clinical trials are research studies conducted to evaluate medical, surgical, or behavioral interventions. These trials are managed by a dedicated research team, which plays a central role in the study process. The research team is responsible for reviewing the study details with participants, ensuring they understand the purpose, procedures, risks, and potential benefits before enrollment. In addition to guiding participants through the informed consent process, the research team actively helps collect research data throughout the trial. They also coordinate patient care, working alongside healthcare providers to ensure that participants receive appropriate medical attention and that the trial protocol is followed. Thus, the research team bridges the gap between clinical care and research, supporting both data integrity and participant well-being. Together, clinical trials and the research team form an integrated framework for advancing medical knowledge while maintaining patient safety and care coordination.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: RESEARCH TEAM
Description: The RESEARCH TEAM is a group of experts responsible for managing clinical trials. Their duties include reviewing the study with participants, explaining the study's purpose, risks, and benefits, as well as collecting research data and coordinating care for patients who are participating in the clinical trial.
Relationships:
  - Source: CARE TEAM
  - Target: RESEARCH TEAM
  - Description: The research team is part of the broader care team for patients in a clinical trial
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIALS
  - Target: RESEARCH TEAM
  - Description: Clinical trials are research studies conducted to evaluate medical, surgical, or behavioral interventions. These trials are managed by a dedicated research team, which plays a central role in the study process. The research team is responsible for reviewing the study details with participants, ensuring they understand the purpose, procedures, risks, and potential benefits before enrollment. In addition to guiding participants through the informed consent process, the research team actively helps collect research data throughout the trial. They also coordinate patient care, working alongside healthcare providers to ensure that participants receive appropriate medical attention and that the trial protocol is followed. Thus, the research team bridges the gap between clinical care and research, supporting both data integrity and participant well-being. Together, clinical trials and the research team form an integrated framework for advancing medical knowledge while maintaining patient safety and care coordination.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANCER CARE TEAM">
      <data key="d0">CANCER CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d1">CANCER CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The cancer care team is the patient's dedicated medical team responsible for guiding and managing cancer treatment. This team decides on the appropriate treatment plan, and as part of its comprehensive care, it performs pregnancy tests before starting any cancer treatment to ensure patient safety. The team also assesses fertility risks associated with the proposed treatment, offering referrals to address fertility preservation or related concerns. In addition, the cancer care team communicates important diagnoses to the patient, such as Richter transformation, ensuring that patients are fully informed about their condition. Overall, this team provides holistic cancer care, encompassing diagnosis, treatment planning, pre-treatment screening, fertility considerations, and ongoing communication throughout the patient's cancer journey.
Relationships: (None listed)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: CANCER CARE TEAM
Description: The cancer care team is the patient's dedicated medical team responsible for guiding and managing cancer treatment. This team decides on the appropriate treatment plan, and as part of its comprehensive care, it performs pregnancy tests before starting any cancer treatment to ensure patient safety. The team also assesses fertility risks associated with the proposed treatment, offering referrals to address fertility preservation or related concerns. In addition, the cancer care team communicates important diagnoses to the patient, such as Richter transformation, ensuring that patients are fully informed about their condition. Overall, this team provides holistic cancer care, encompassing diagnosis, treatment planning, pre-treatment screening, fertility considerations, and ongoing communication throughout the patient's cancer journey.
Relationships: (None listed)</data>
    </node>
