    <node id="SOURCE: BIOPSY → TARGET: CARE TEAM — THE CARE TEAM COMMONLY REQUESTS A BIOPSY SAMPLE TO CONFIRM A DIAGNOSIS OF GLIOMA. IN ADDITION, THE CARE TEAM USES THE RESULTS FROM THAT BIOPSY TO HELP DETERMINE THE PATIENT'S CANCER RISK. TOGETHER, THE BIOPSY AND THE CARE TEAM ARE CLOSELY CONNECTED: THE BIOPSY PROVIDES ESSENTIAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION, WHILE THE CARE TEAM RELIES ON THIS INFORMATION BOTH TO CONFIRM THE PRESENCE OF GLIOMA AND TO ASSESS THE OVERALL RISK ASSOCIATED WITH THE CANCER.">
