      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14. Source: CARE TEAM → Target: PATIENT — The CARE TEAM and the PATIENT work together as partners in the patient’s healthcare journey. The care team is responsible for assembling and reviewing test results, using this information to manage and coordinate the patient’s ongoing care. In this collaborative relationship, the patient actively participates by discussing test results with the care team and following the recommendations provided. The patient is encouraged to communicate openly with the care team, share symptoms and concerns, and help the care team get to know them as an individual. In return, the care team provides care, guidance, and management based on the patient’s unique needs. Together, the CARE TEAM and the PATIENT form a cooperative unit focused on achieving the best possible health outcomes.</data>
    </node>
