      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is a U.S. federal regulatory agency responsible for approving drugs, devices, and treatment approaches after they have been demonstrated to be safe and effective in clinical trials. It may also approve investigational treatments, including those used in clinical trials, under its regulatory authority. As the key oversight body in the United States, the FDA evaluates clinical trial data to determine whether a medical product or treatment approach meets the required standards for safety and efficacy before it can be made available to the public.
Relationships:
  - (No explicit relationships listed in the data for this entity beyond its description.)

---</data>
