      <data key="d3">Informed consent is the process through which a research team explains the purpose, risks, and benefits of a clinical trial to a prospective participant. During this process, the participant reviews the details of the trial and subsequently signs an informed consent form before enrolling. In some cases, the research team presents this information and the participant reviews and signs the consent form as part of the enrollment procedure.
