    <node id="PHASE 4 TRIALS">
      <data key="d0">PHASE 4 TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d1">PHASE 4 TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Phase 4 trials are a phase of clinical research that study the long-term safety and benefit of an FDA-approved treatment. These trials are conducted after a treatment has already received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration, focusing on monitoring its real-world effectiveness and any potential side effects over an extended period. As clinical trials, Phase 4 trials help gather additional information on how the treatment performs in a broader patient population, ensuring that its benefits continue to outweigh any risks in everyday medical practice.
Relationships:
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: PHASE 4 TRIALS
  - Description: Phase 4 trials are a phase of clinical trials studying long-term safety and benefit after FDA approval

---</data>
