    <node id="CHEMOTHERAPY → CHEMORADIATION">
      <data key="d0">CHEMOTHERAPY → CHEMORADIATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CHEMOTHERAPY → CHEMORADIATION</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Chemotherapy is a cancer treatment that uses drugs to kill or slow the growth of cancer cells. Chemoradiation is a treatment approach that combines chemotherapy with radiation therapy. In this combined regimen, chemotherapy serves as one of the core components, specifically functioning as the chemotherapy portion of the treatment. Chemoradiation may be followed by additional chemotherapy, which is given to kill any lingering cancer cells that remain after the initial combined treatment.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
