    <node id="SKIN EXAM">
      <data key="d0">SKIN EXAM</data>
      <data key="d1">SKIN EXAM</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A skin exam is a procedure performed by dermatologists to evaluate the skin for various conditions, with a primary focus on detecting skin cancer. During this examination, dermatologists thoroughly inspect the skin for any suspicious lesions, growths, or abnormalities that may indicate cancerous or precancerous changes. In addition to conducting the examination, dermatologists also educate patients on how to perform skin self-exams, enabling them to monitor their own skin between professional visits. The skin exam is an integral component of the diagnostic evaluation and ongoing follow-up for basal cell skin cancer, helping to identify the disease, assess its extent, and monitor for recurrence or new lesions. Overall, it serves as both a preventive screening tool and a key part of managing existing skin cancer diagnoses.
Relationships: None listed.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
