      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">A radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in interpreting imaging tests, including positron emission tomography (PET) scans. The radiologist reads and analyzes PET images to provide diagnostic information that helps guide patient care. PET scans are a form of nuclear medicine imaging that produce detailed images of functional processes in the body, and the radiologist plays a key role in interpreting these images to identify abnormalities and support clinical decisions.
Relationships:
  - Source: PET SCAN
  - Target: RADIOLOGIST
  - Description: A radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in interpreting imaging tests, including positron emission tomography (PET) scans. The radiologist reads and analyzes PET images to provide diagnostic information that helps guide patient care. PET scans are a form of nuclear medicine imaging that produce detailed images of functional processes in the body, and the radiologist plays a key role in interpreting these images to identify abnormalities and support clinical decisions.

---</data>
