    <node id="CIRRHOSIS">
      <data key="d0">CIRRHOSIS</data>
      <data key="d1">CIRRHOSIS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease characterized by scarring of the liver. It is recognized as a known and major risk factor for liver cancer, and as such, it serves as an important indication for liver cancer screening. Risk assessments for liver cancer often compare individuals with cirrhosis to those without the condition, highlighting the elevated risk associated with the disease.
Relationships:
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER CANCER SCREENING
  - Description: People with cirrhosis should be enrolled in a liver cancer screening program.</data>
