    <node id="INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS">
      <data key="d0">INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS</data>
      <data key="d1">INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics (FIGO) is a professional organization best known for developing the FIGO staging system, a standardized framework used to classify the extent of gynecological cancers. This system is widely adopted in clinical practice and is considered the most commonly used staging method for both ovarian cancer and cervical cancer. For ovarian cancer, the FIGO staging system is similar to the AJCC (American Joint Committee on Cancer) system, and it serves as the primary tool for determining disease progression and guiding treatment decisions. For cervical cancer, FIGO similarly provides the definitive staging criteria, ensuring consistent evaluation and communication among healthcare providers worldwide. By establishing these staging systems, FIGO has played a central role in advancing the diagnosis, treatment, and research of gynecologic malignancies. Its staging classifications are integral to oncology practice, enabling accurate prognosis and comparison of treatment outcomes across different clinical settings.

**Relationships:**
  - Source: AMERICAN JOINT COMMITTEE ON CANCER
  - Target: INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS
  - Description: The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and the International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics (FIGO) have both developed staging systems for ovarian cancer. The two systems are similar in structure and intent, providing standardized frameworks for classifying the extent of the disease. Although both staging systems are recognized and used in clinical practice, the FIGO system is employed most often. This reflects its widespread acceptance and practical utility in the management and communication of ovarian cancer cases.

---</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS
Description: The International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics (FIGO) is a professional organization best known for developing the FIGO staging system, a standardized framework used to classify the extent of gynecological cancers. This system is widely adopted in clinical practice and is considered the most commonly used staging method for both ovarian cancer and cervical cancer. For ovarian cancer, the FIGO staging system is similar to the AJCC (American Joint Committee on Cancer) system, and it serves as the primary tool for determining disease progression and guiding treatment decisions. For cervical cancer, FIGO similarly provides the definitive staging criteria, ensuring consistent evaluation and communication among healthcare providers worldwide. By establishing these staging systems, FIGO has played a central role in advancing the diagnosis, treatment, and research of gynecologic malignancies. Its staging classifications are integral to oncology practice, enabling accurate prognosis and comparison of treatment outcomes across different clinical settings.

**Relationships:**
  - Source: AMERICAN JOINT COMMITTEE ON CANCER
  - Target: INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS
  - Description: The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and the International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics (FIGO) have both developed staging systems for ovarian cancer. The two systems are similar in structure and intent, providing standardized frameworks for classifying the extent of the disease. Although both staging systems are recognized and used in clinical practice, the FIGO system is employed most often. This reflects its widespread acceptance and practical utility in the management and communication of ovarian cancer cases.

---</data>
    </node>
