    <node id="BRACHYTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">BRACHYTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d1">BRACHYTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Brachytherapy is a form of radiation therapy in which a radioactive source is placed close to, in direct contact with, or inside the tumor or body. As an internal radiation therapy, it delivers a high radiation dose directly to the tumor while limiting exposure to surrounding healthy tissue. Brachytherapy is commonly used in the treatment of cervical cancer, including as an internal radiation treatment after surgery or for pelvic recurrence. For locally advanced cervical cancer, it is recommended in combination with chemoradiation.
Relationships:
