  - Target: HYSTERECTOMY AND BSO
  - Description: Information gained during surgery contributes to determining the pathologic stage of ovarian cancer
  - Source: GENERAL ANESTHESIA
  - Target: HYSTERECTOMY AND BSO
  - Description: General anesthesia is given so the patient can undergo hysterectomy and BSO without pain
  - Source: PREMATURE MENOPAUSE
  - Target: HYSTERECTOMY AND BSO
  - Description: Surgery that removes both ovaries causes premature menopause if the patient has not already entered menopause
  - Source: BLOOD THINNERS
  - Target: HYSTERECTOMY AND BSO
  - Description: Many patients are placed on blood thinners for up to 4 weeks after hysterectomy and BSO to help prevent blood clots
  - Source: DEEP VEIN THROMBOSIS
  - Target: HYSTERECTOMY AND BSO
  - Description: Recent abdominal surgery is a risk factor for developing deep vein thrombosis, so surgery patients are monitored for blood clots</data>
