      <data key="d3">APL (acute promyelocytic leukemia) is a rare subtype of acute myeloid leukemia (AML). It is characterized by the abnormal fusion gene PML::RARA, which results from a translocation between chromosomes 15 and 17. This genetic abnormality is a defining feature of the disease and drives its clinical behavior. APL is discussed in Chapter 5 of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which provides information about this specific leukemia subtype. As a distinct form of AML, APL requires specialized diagnostic evaluation and management approaches due to its unique genetic basis and clinical characteristics.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
