    <node id="IMAGING TEST">
      <data key="d0">IMAGING TEST</data>
      <data key="d1">IMAGING TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">An imaging test is a diagnostic scan used to determine whether cancer has spread beyond a suspicious lesion into bone, nerves, or surrounding deep soft tissue. It produces pictures of the inside of the body, revealing cancer size, location, spread, and response to treatment. Common methods include MRI, CT, PET, ultrasound, and bone scan. Imaging tests may also be ordered if a doctor suspects that cancer has come back or spread, such as with CT scans.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: IMAGING TEST
  - Target: (various cancer types and clinical contexts as described in the report)</data>
