    <node id="FDG-PET/CT">
      <data key="d0">FDG-PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d1">FDG-PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">FDG-PET/CT is a specialized imaging procedure that combines a positron emission tomography (PET) scan with computed tomography (CT). As a type of PET/CT scan, it inherently includes a PET scan component, which is integrated with CT to provide both functional and anatomical information. The technique utilizes a radiotracer—specifically fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG)—to detect glucose uptake, which is particularly useful for identifying cancer cells due to their heightened metabolic activity. In summary, FDG-PET/CT is a PET scan combined with CT that leverages FDG to visualize glucose metabolism, making it a valuable tool in oncology and other medical applications.
Relationships:
  - Source: PET SCAN
  - Target: FDG-PET/CT
  - Description: FDG-PET/CT is a specialized imaging procedure that combines a positron emission tomography (PET) scan with computed tomography (CT). As a type of PET/CT scan, it inherently includes a PET scan component, which is integrated with CT to provide both functional and anatomical information. The technique utilizes a radiotracer—specifically fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG)—to detect glucose uptake, which is particularly useful for identifying cancer cells due to their heightened metabolic activity. In summary, FDG-PET/CT is a PET scan combined with CT that leverages FDG to visualize glucose metabolism, making it a valuable tool in oncology and other medical applications.

---</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: FDG-PET/CT
Description: FDG-PET/CT is a specialized imaging procedure that combines a positron emission tomography (PET) scan with computed tomography (CT). As a type of PET/CT scan, it inherently includes a PET scan component, which is integrated with CT to provide both functional and anatomical information. The technique utilizes a radiotracer—specifically fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG)—to detect glucose uptake, which is particularly useful for identifying cancer cells due to their heightened metabolic activity. In summary, FDG-PET/CT is a PET scan combined with CT that leverages FDG to visualize glucose metabolism, making it a valuable tool in oncology and other medical applications.
Relationships:
  - Source: PET SCAN
  - Target: FDG-PET/CT
