    <node id="OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER">
      <data key="d0">OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER</data>
      <data key="d1">OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Oropharyngeal cancer, also called throat (oropharyngeal) cancer, is a cancer of the oropharynx, the middle part of the throat near the mouth. It is classified as a head and neck cancer. The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient guidelines and patient information for this condition.
Relationships:
  - Source: HEAD AND NECK CANCER
  - Target: OROPHARYNGEAL CANCER
  - Description: Oropharyngeal cancer is a type of head and neck cancer that arises in the oropharynx, which is part of the throat. Head and neck cancer is a broader category of malignancies, and oropharyngeal cancer represents a specific subtype originating in the oropharynx.</data>
