      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Using CT scan pictures, the radiation team plans the radiation dose and number of treatments</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIATION THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIATION THERAPY" target="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADIATION THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Radiation therapy and systemic therapy are both treatment options for squamous cell skin cancer. They may be used together, as radiation therapy can be given with certain systemic therapies, and systemic therapy may be given in addition to radiation therapy. Systemic therapy may also be considered as an option if surgery and radiation therapy are not possible or were not successful.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIATION THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
