    <edge source="BURKITT LYMPHOMA" target="NON-HODGKIN LYMPHOMA" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">BURKITT LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d8">NON-HODGKIN LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Burkitt lymphoma is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma. This means that Burkitt lymphoma belongs to the broader classification of non-Hodgkin lymphoma, which encompasses a diverse group of blood cancers that arise from lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell. As a non-Hodgkin lymphoma, Burkitt lymphoma shares certain characteristics with other lymphomas in this category, such as its origin in the lymphatic system, but it also has distinct clinical and pathological features. The classification of Burkitt lymphoma as a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma is fundamental to understanding its diagnosis, treatment approach, and prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d12">NON-HODGKIN LYMPHOMA</data>
    </edge>
